From: Asdlerto Korry <korryasdlerto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qrtrqmi, qmimodem/sim: M52XQ dual SIM (DSDS) - second modem for subscription 1

The SoC modem of the Samsung Galaxy M52 has two subscriptions behind one
QRTR node. The udev modem (subscription 0) creates a second ofono modem for
subscription 1 once it is powered. Each modem binds its NAS, VOICE and WMS
clients to its subscription; the SIM driver gets the subscription as vendor
and uses the primary / secondary GW provisioning session, the matching card
status index and the PIN card session of its slot. IMSI of SIM 2 is read from
EF IMSI. The data path (IPA, gprs, lte) and the modem operating mode stay
with the first modem. The slot driver registers two slots.
---
--- a/plugins/qrtrqmi.c	2026-11-15 02:08:51.873089520 +0200
+++ b/plugins/qrtrqmi.c	2026-11-15 02:09:52.429426820 +0200
